{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbCmdP2ShA7hCWM26iPm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the three candidate files, and the self-check passes (`OK`). It can't fully vouch for the model, though: it's a single short smoke fit, so the novelty and convergence gates haven't been run.\n\n**Model:** `palindrome_aversion_terminal_streak_lapse`, a refinement of the incumbent `terminal_run_streak_aversion_lapse`.\n\n**The one change:** people treat mirror symmetry as a sign that a sequence was designed. A sequence that reads the same both ways (e.g. HTTTTTTH, HHHTTHHH) looks less random by one shared, fitted weight. Everything else is the incumbent unchanged: each person's own ideal switching rate, their own weights against lopsided heads/tails counts and against the longest streak, the shared weight on the final streak, and their own guessing rate.\n\n**Why this change:** it targets the strongest discrepancy in the critique, the one with the largest gap that still counts after correcting for testing several statistics at once (z = −5.86, q = 0.016). Where exactly one sequence in a pair is a palindrome, people chose it 49% of the time, but the incumbent predicts 53.6%. I left the other significant discrepancy, about the streak a sequence starts on, alone to keep this to a single change.\n\n**Self-check result:** the model loads, its log-probability is finite and it follows the data contract. ELPD-LOO came out at −2336.2 against the incumbent's −2378.9. That figure comes from one chain of 100 draws, so it is not comparable with the incumbent's full fit and is not evidence that this model wins. The check also warned that PSIS-LOO is unreliable on this short fit (6.9% of trials have a high Pareto k, above the 1% tolerance).\n\n**Still to come at admission:**\n- **Novelty:** palindromes are only part of the stimulus space, so the model's predictions may not differ enough from the incumbent's to pass.\n- **Convergence:** the full fit has to meet the divergence, R-hat and ESS limits.\n- **Speed:** each sampling run has a 30-minute limit. The smoke fit sampled in 36 seconds.\n\nFiles are in `experiment2/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_4/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2699,"cache_read_input_tokens":65826,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2699,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35b2fb86-cfab-48c6-92da-12d11f1ab171","uuid":"528c0b4a-9d13-40e2-8da8-822768992be1","timestamp":"2026-10-01T08:30:08.398Z","request_id":"req_011CfbCmcsmAZZLYQjHykzSC"}
